# problem #15, a regression found on the first GPU run (nvtest fgprio on the
# RTX 5000, 2026-11-11): a Chrome whose WebGL memory is hundreds of 6 MB
# contiguous buffers. Counted as "buffers that need a window", they came back
# 256 MB a step (11 s instead of 0.7 s) and the last ones never. Only buffers
# of 32 MB or more wait for a window; these come back as any other memory.
cap 11000
set longest 64
proc 1614 kwin_wayland old
proc 2617 chrome old chunk=16
proc 12557 game old chunk=64

act 1614 0 4
mark the browser alone, focused: 1.2 GB in 6 MB contiguous buffers
hint 2617 f
act 2617 0 20
alloc 2617 1200 n=200 contig
at 6

mark the game takes the focus and nearly all of vidmem: the browser, hidden, pays
hint 2617 h
hint 12557 f
act 12557 0 30
act 2617 30 0
target 12557 10850 0.75 spread=20
at 40
expect evicted 2617 >= 800

mark back to the browser, the game stays visible on the other monitor
hint 12557 v
hint 2617 f
act 2617 0 20
step
step
expect evicted 2617 <= 64        # back within two steps, not 256 MB a step
at 60
expect evicted 2617 == 0
expect windows 2617 == 0         # no window for small buffers
